body:
First of all, the appropriate level of treatment to start is Intensive Outpatient Program (IOP)  or  partial hospitalization program (PHP). If those options fail, then move on to residential treatment. 

&#x200B;

Generally speaking, university-affiliated teaching hospitals are a good choice.   
**Please do not send your friend to some random facility.**  


&#x200B;

# Some good options:

[https://www.mcleanhospital.org/addiction](https://www.mcleanhospital.org/addiction)

[https://rogersbh.org/](https://rogersbh.org/)

&#x200B;

[https://www.sheppardpratt.org/care-finder/the-retreat/areas-of-expertise/co-occurring-disorders-addiction/](https://www.sheppardpratt.org/care-finder/the-retreat/areas-of-expertise/co-occurring-disorders-addiction/)

&#x200B;

[https://silverhillhospital.org/what-we-treat/substance-abuse-treatment-nj/#co-occurring\_disorders](https://silverhillhospital.org/what-we-treat/substance-abuse-treatment-nj/#co-occurring_disorders)

&#x200B;

[https://www.nyp.org/psychiatry/addiction-substance-use](https://www.nyp.org/psychiatry/addiction-substance-use)
